{"id": "EUVD-2026-81875", "enisaUuid": "f8d8b184-b5d0-30cf-b210-f551c16a3153", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nphy: qcom: qmp-usb-legacy: Fix possible NULL-deref on early runtime suspend\n\nThere is a small window where the runtime suspend callback may run\nafter pm_runtime_enable() and before pm_runtime_forbid(). In this\ncase, a crash occurs because runtime suspend/resume dereferences\nqmp->phy pointer, which is not yet initialized:\n        `if (!qmp->phy->init_count) {`\n\nThis can also happen if user re-enables runtime-pm via the sysfs\nattribute before qmp phy is initialized.\n\nSimilarly to other qcom phy drivers, introduce a qmp->phy_initialized\nvariable that can be used to avoid relying on the possibly uninitialized\nphy pointer.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:01:00", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/602059c5128a78857ca92bd22791ab640185e381", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/29449ce1f5958e36df80318878016e3ecac26b40", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/52ad86ea5f98d29a7a29d9ba12e24276c6e30acd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f9789d1b63e7d9f868ac9c29564339a4c03ceb5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8e3687f7e18fe84372e86875709d56c37e7525a8"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hprq-7rq9-g5cm", "CVE-2026-90282"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "19c1d205-a444-3368-8e0b-7b7d4475c7e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e464a3180a43b6596bd267f9f274e1793bfb8150 <29449ce1f5958e36df80318878016e3ecac26b40"}, {"id": "374ad422-ff3b-325f-a45f-f338628a888d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "64a2114e-d78b-385d-8284-0c62d6262906", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e464a3180a43b6596bd267f9f274e1793bfb8150 <602059c5128a78857ca92bd22791ab640185e381"}, {"id": "71eccaee-e2b8-3220-b643-b782d951656f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "9574dfa9-d696-3b58-be52-f655fc324456", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6"}, {"id": "a9a73548-ab90-3030-8e06-245e6dbee8d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e464a3180a43b6596bd267f9f274e1793bfb8150 <8e3687f7e18fe84372e86875709d56c37e7525a8"}, {"id": "ca6a87f7-20be-375e-b2f3-40187a2a83bf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "ca7b1bac-15a6-398a-a746-35894c0f8814", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "cebe878b-aba2-35c0-a0cf-df8d233d0859", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "d2331c41-812a-339e-8ce9-36396f8476e4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e464a3180a43b6596bd267f9f274e1793bfb8150 <0f9789d1b63e7d9f868ac9c29564339a4c03ceb5"}, {"id": "d8f51d29-ae85-3059-aa8e-f16cc73f72b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ee03ab05-6c8b-3040-881a-d3fedf2e1c20", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e464a3180a43b6596bd267f9f274e1793bfb8150 <52ad86ea5f98d29a7a29d9ba12e24276c6e30acd"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c4b121d6-409f-3723-bb42-a6a678de8ce6", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}